; ======================================================================
;  BRANCHES. The offset is the low byte, signed, in words:
;      PC = PC + 2 * offset
;  written without a branch as ((Op & $FF) << 1) - ((Op & $80) << 2).
;  Each branch owns 32 table entries (its offset spills into bits 7-3).
; ======================================================================

;-BR--------------------------------------------------------------------
